    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1219">

                <pb facs="1212" n="926" xml:id="pg926"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/1457</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-02-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 26, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received March 10, 8.10 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1610. Your telegram February 4 to Consul Jerusalem. Foreign Office informs
                    Embassy that medical supplies for Jewish hospital in Jerusalem may be landed by
                    collier at Jaffa upon condition that no member of crew goes ashore and that no
                    one, not even American consulate official, goes on board collier. Have so
                    informed Jerusalem. Telegraph probable date arrival.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
